    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><font color=\"#202124\" face=\"Roboto, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgba(32,33,36,0.04)\"><br></span></font></div><div><font color=\"#202124\" face=\"Roboto, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">Hi Filipe,</span></font></div><div><font color=\"#202124\" face=\"Roboto, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgba(32,33,36,0.04)\"><br></span></font></div><span style=\"color:rgb(32,33,36);font-family:Roboto,sans-serif;font-size:14px;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgba(32,33,36,0.04)\"><div>I am working on developing an algorithm for wheat ear count detection from drone imagery. The resolution of our images is 0.19 cm/pixel. Reference reprints followed were Zhao et al., 2021 (<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.3390/rs13163095\" style=\"color:rgba(56,112,46,0.75);box-sizing:border-box;line-height:inherit;text-decoration-line:none;font-weight:700;font-family:Arial;font-size:12px\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://doi.org/10.3390/rs13163095&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793241902662000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0gMHJ3DJyAVhaxrYTj50MS\">https://doi.org/10.3390/rs13163095</a>) and Zhan et al., 2022 (<span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(34,34,34)\"><a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00500-021-06407-8\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://doi.org/10.1007/s00500-021-06407-8&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793241902662000&amp;usg=AOvVaw18tlGTi1Piv8FjfhtvfSF9\">https://doi.org/10.1007/s00500-021-06407-8</a> </span>). </div><div><br></div><div>We have annotated 5 drone images to see the detection. Each image has approx.5k annotations. We were using <span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(34,34,34)\">Model: Yolov5 , (s , m, l ,x ,5v6 ,5s6, 5m6 ,5l6, 5x6 ) and yolox</span>. But detection of the wheat ear was a challenge. I would like to get some suggestions for better detection especially for feature extraction architecture (backbone) in wheat ears through any online platforms.<br></div></span><div><span style=\"background-color:rgba(32,33,36,0.04);color:rgb(32,33,36);font-family:Roboto,sans-serif;font-size:14px;white-space:pre-wrap\"><br></span></div><div>Kindly suggest the techniques for feature extraction of the wheat ear.<span style=\"background-color:rgba(32,33,36,0.04);color:rgb(32,33,36);font-family:Roboto,sans-serif;font-size:14px;white-space:pre-wrap\"><br></span></div><div><br></div><div>Thank you,</div><div>Sudhir.</div><div><br></div></div>\r\n"
    ]
   ]
  },
